      excerpt: "Your contractor says 3 months. Reality says 8. The honest timeline for building a house in Ghana plus strategies to prevent delays.",
      content: `<p>Every contractor promises fast delivery. Most projects run 2-5 months behind schedule. Here is the realistic timeline for building in Ghana in 2026.</p><h2>Realistic Timelines by House Type</h2><p><strong>2-bedroom:</strong> 4-8 months. <strong>3-bedroom:</strong> 6-10 months. <strong>4-bedroom:</strong> 8-14 months. <strong>5-bedroom+:</strong> 10-18 months.</p><h2>Why Projects Get Delayed</h2><p>Funding gaps (most common cause): 40% of delays. Material availability: 20%. Contractor scheduling: 15%. Weather (rainy season): 15%. Permit issues: 10%.</p><h2>How to Stay on Schedule</h2><p>Secure full funding before starting. Order materials in advance. Build during dry season (November-March). Hire a dedicated project manager. Include penalty clauses in contractor contract.</p><p>Plan your build timeline and budget with our free calculator.</p>`,
