      slug: "phased-house-building-ghana",
      excerpt: "Most Ghanaians do not have the full build budget upfront. Here is the smart way to build in phases without wasting money.",
      content: `<p>Building in phases is how most Ghanaians actually build. You start with what you have, get to a safe stopping point, then continue when more funds are available. Here is how to do it right.</p><h2>Phase 1: Foundation and Structure (40% of Budget)</h2><p>Site clearing, foundation, walls, columns, lintels, and roof structure. Get the house watertight and secure. Cost for a 3-bedroom: GHS 250,000–400,000.</p><h2>Phase 2: Roofing and Rough-In (25% of Budget)</h2><p>Roof covering, windows, doors, plumbing rough-in, electrical rough-in. Cost: GHS 150,000–250,000.</p><h2>Phase 3: Finishing (35% of Budget)</h2><p>Plastering, flooring, painting, kitchen installation, bathroom fitting, final electrical and plumbing. Cost: GHS 200,000–350,000.</p><h2>Smart Phasing Tips</h2><p>Always finish to roof level first before pausing. An unroofed structure deteriorates quickly. Store materials securely between phases. Keep receipts and records for continuous work.</p><p>Plan your phased build with our free cost calculator.</p>`,
