      excerpt: "Living abroad and planning to build in Ghana? Everything diaspora builders need to know about remote construction management.",
      content: `<p>Building in Ghana while living abroad is challenging but thousands do it successfully. Here is a complete guide for diaspora builders.</p><h2>Choose the Right Team</h2><p>You need people on the ground you can trust. Hire a project manager or quantity surveyor as your representative. They inspect work, pay artisans, buy materials, and report to you weekly.</p><h2>Use Technology</h2><p>Require weekly video updates and photos. Use WhatsApp groups for daily communication. Google Earth for site monitoring. Mobile money for payments.</p><h2>Legal Protection</h2><p>Power of attorney to a trusted relative or lawyer. Detailed contracts with penalty clauses. Escrow payments through a lawyer's account.</p><h2>Common Diaspora Mistakes</h2><p>Trusting relatives to manage without experience. Sending too much money at once. Not visiting during critical stages (foundation pouring, roofing).</p><p>Plan your diaspora build with our comprehensive cost calculator.</p>`,
