      title: "Solar Power for Houses in Ghana 2026: Cost, Benefits, and Installation Guide",
      slug: "solar-power-houses-ghana-2026",
      excerpt: "Stop paying ECG bills forever. The real cost of installing solar power for your house in Ghana including panels, batteries, and inverters.",
      content: `<p>With rising electricity costs and unreliable grid supply, solar power is becoming a smart investment for Ghanaian homeowners. Here is exactly what it costs in 2026.</p><h2>Solar System Costs by Size</h2><p><strong>Basic (lights, TV, phone charging):</strong> GHS 8,000–15,000. 500W panels, 1.5kVA inverter, 2 batteries.</p><p><strong>Standard (full home, no AC):</strong> GHS 20,000–40,000. 1.5kW panels, 3kVA inverter, 4 batteries.</p><p><strong>Premium (full home with AC):</strong> GHS 50,000–120,000. 5kW+ panels, 8kVA+ inverter, 8+ batteries.</p><h2>Payback Period</h2><p>With ECG electricity costs at GHS 1.2/kWh and rising, a standard solar system pays for itself in 3-5 years. After that, your electricity is free.</p><h2>Installation Tips</h2><p>Use lithium-ion batteries (longer lifespan, lighter). Hire a licensed solar installer. Get grid-tied with battery backup for the best of both worlds.</p><p>Include solar in your build budget using our free calculator.</p>`,
